  "content": {
    "id": "p57-q13-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p57-q13-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2-9}{x^2-6x+9}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{x+3}{x-3}$, $x\\ne3$.",
          "worked": "The original denominator requires $x\\ne3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-9}{x^2-6x+9}&=\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{(x-3)^2}\\\\\\frac{x^2-9}{x^2-6x+9}&=\\frac{x+3}{x-3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q14-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3x}{x-2}-\\dfrac6{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3(x^2+4)}{x^2-4}$, $x\\ne-2,2$.\n\nUse the common denominator $(x-2)(x+2)$.",
          "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-2,2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3x(x+2)-6(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3x^2+6x-6x+12}{x^2-4}\\\\\\frac{3x}{x-2}-\\frac6{x+2}&=\\frac{3(x^2+4)}{x^2-4}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q15-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac2x+\\dfrac3{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{5x-2}{x(x-1)}$, $x\\ne0,1$.",
          "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne0,1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2x+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{2(x-1)+3x}{x(x-1)}\\\\\\frac2x+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{5x-2}{x(x-1)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q16-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5x-10}{x^2-25}\\div\\dfrac{x-2}{x+5}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac5{x-5}$, $x\\ne-5,2,5$.\n\nMultiply by the reciprocal, then factorise and cancel.",
          "worked": "The original denominators exclude $x=-5,5$. The divisor must also be nonzero, so $x\\ne2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5x-10}{x^2-25}\\div\\frac{x-2}{x+5}&=\\frac{5(x-2)}{(x-5)(x+5)}\\times\\frac{x+5}{x-2}\\\\\\frac{5x-10}{x^2-25}\\div\\frac{x-2}{x+5}&=\\frac5{x-5}.\\end{align*}$$\nDomain: $x\\ne-5,2,5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
